counterfactuals.output:
A smart lighting system comprising:

a plurality of lighting devices, each lighting device including at least one electrical load configured to generate illumination;

a plurality of transceiver modules, each transceiver module being electrically coupled to a corresponding one of the electrical loads and configured to control delivery of power to the corresponding electrical load;

a memory associated with each transceiver module, the memory storing identification data uniquely associated with the corresponding lighting device and security data configured to authenticate communications with the corresponding transceiver module; and

a controller configured to manage operation of the plurality of lighting devices, the controller including:

a first communication interface configured to communicate with the plurality of transceiver modules using a local lighting-control communication protocol; and

a second communication interface configured to communicate with an external network or user device using a network communication protocol different from the local lighting-control communication protocol;

wherein the controller is configured to receive, via the second communication interface, a lighting control command or configuration instruction, authenticate at least one transceiver module using the stored security data, identify the corresponding lighting device using the stored identification data, and transmit, via the first communication interface, a control signal to the authenticated transceiver module to adjust operation of the corresponding electrical load.

In some embodiments, the electrical load comprises one or more light-emitting diodes, lamps, drivers, dimming circuits, sensors, or auxiliary loads. The stored security data may include an encryption key, certificate, token, password, or authentication credential. The controller may be further configured to associate the identification data with a physical location, lighting zone, fixture type, user profile, or commissioning record, and to selectively control intensity, color temperature, color, timing, occupancy response, daylight response, or power state of the lighting devices based on the received command or configuration instruction.
